<h1>B*-tree</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="btree.html"><em>B-tree</em></a> in which <a href="node.html"><em>nodes</em></a> are kept 2/3 full by redistributing <a href="key.html"><em>keys</em></a> to fill two <a href="child.html"><em>child</em></a> nodes, then splitting them into three nodes.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bplustree.html"><em>B<sup>+</sup>-tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
See links at B-tree.
</p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

